      en: "The Gishora Kids Drumming School is located near Gitega, Burundi's political capital. Founded in 1995, it teaches the traditional Burundian drumming art (Ingoma) to children aged 6-14. Drums are handmade from wood and animal skins. The school hosts about 50 active students and performs regularly at cultural events. In 2014, Burundi's royal drumming was recognized by UNESCO as an Intangible Cultural Heritage. The school also offers workshops for visitors. Performances feature colorful costumes and choreographed dances. The school plays a key role in preserving Burundian cultural identity.",
